---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SlimNav from "../components/SlimNav.astro";
import SubPageNav from "../components/SubPageNav.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use — Digital Ink"
  description="Terms of use for Digital Ink: Smart Inks, nearby Ink transfers, tokens, optional online AI features and your content."
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
  pageType="article"
  keywords={["Digital Ink terms of use", "Smart Ink", "Ink transfer", "Q888"]}
>
  <SubPageNav />
  <div class="hidden md:block"><SlimNav /></div>

  <main class="policy-page">
    <header class="policy-hero">
      <div class="policy-shell">
        <p class="policy-kicker">DIGITAL INK · PUBLIC RECORD · TERMS</p>
        <h1>Terms<br />of Use</h1>
        <p class="policy-summary">Digital Ink is an art application that works mainly on your iPad. These terms explain how Inks, transfers, tokens and optional online features work, and what you can and cannot expect from them.</p>
        <dl class="policy-meta">
          <div><dt>Effective date</dt><dd>November 21, 2026</dd></div>
          <div><dt>App</dt><dd>Digital Ink</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Developer</dt><dd>Alexander Sestakovs</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Contact</dt><dd><a href="mailto:hello@q888.space">hello@q888.space</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="policy-principles" aria-label="Terms summary">
          <span>Your images stay yours</span><span>Inks are never copied</span><span>Tokens have no cash value</span><span>Online AI is optional</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="policy-shell policy-layout">
      <aside class="policy-toc" aria-label="Terms contents">
        <p>CONTENTS</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#agreement">Agreement</a></li>
          <li><a href="#your-content">Your content</a></li>
          <li><a href="#inks">Smart Inks</a></li>
          <li><a href="#transfers">Ink transfers</a></li>
          <li><a href="#set-free">Set Free and deletion</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tokens">Tokens and purchases</a></li>
          <li><a href="#online">Online features and AI</a></li>
          <li><a href="#verification">Verification and provenance</a></li>
          <li><a href="#use">Acceptable use</a></li>
          <li><a href="#liability">Warranty and liability</a></li>
          <li><a href="#changes">Changes and law</a></li>
        </ol>
      </aside>

      <article class="policy-content">
        <section id="agreement">
          <span class="section-number">01</span><h2>Agreement</h2>
          <p>By downloading or using Digital Ink you agree to these terms and to Apple’s Standard End User License Agreement for apps from the App Store. If the two conflict, Apple’s agreement applies to the licence of the app itself, and these terms apply to how Digital Ink’s features work.</p>
          <p>The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains what information is processed and forms part of these terms.</p>
          <p>Digital Ink is an ongoing artwork and an experiment. It is offered for creative and personal use.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="your-content">
          <span class="section-number">02</span><h2>Your content</h2>
          <p>You keep all rights in the photographs, drawings, PDFs and other material you choose to import. Digital Ink does not claim ownership of your material or of the artworks you make.</p>
          <p>Only import material you have the right to use. You are responsible for what you import, draw, export, share or transfer, including material that shows other people.</p>
          <p>Digital Ink stores your Inks and artworks on your iPad. It is your responsibility to export what you want to keep. Deleting the app, resetting its data or losing the device can remove local data that has not been exported or backed up.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="inks">
          <span class="section-number">03</span><h2>Smart Inks</h2>
          <p>A Smart Ink is a record created from one imported image. It has one colour, a finite supply of that colour, an origin and a growing history. Each Ink is in one place at a time: Ink Home, Canvas or Gallery.</p>
          <p>Painting spends the Ink; erasing returns it. Digital Ink is designed so that an Ink cannot be duplicated and so that every painted pixel links to the Ink that made it. A collection holds up to 1,000 Inks on one iPad.</p>
          <p class="policy-emphasis">Inks are not money, securities or investments. They have no guaranteed value, and Digital Ink makes no promise that an Ink can be sold, exchanged or recovered. Inks are not claimed to be alive or intelligent.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="transfers">
          <span class="section-number">04</span><h2>Ink transfers</h2>
          <p>Ink Transfer moves one eligible Ink at a time between two artists’ iPads that are nearby. Both artists need an Artist Identity, must allow Local Network access, and must compare and confirm the same pairing code. The receiver reviews a preview and accepts before the sender sends the Ink.</p>
          <p>A transfer moves the Ink; it does not copy it. When a transfer completes, the Ink leaves the sender’s collection and belongs to the receiver, together with its biography, learning and provenance. It can also include personal notes, a Source Memory image, a reconstruction preview and recorded photo details such as location. Check the Ink’s BIO before choosing it.</p>
          <p>A completed transfer cannot be undone by Digital Ink. Only transfer to people you intend to give the Ink to. If a connection drops, you can resume from Transfer history on both iPads while the records exist. Transfer records and receipts remain on both iPads.</p>
          <p>Moving a whole collection, and recovering Inks after a lost, reset or deleted iPad, are not currently available. Digital Ink cannot restore Inks that are no longer on a device.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="set-free">
          <span class="section-number">05</span><h2>Set Free and deletion</h2>
          <p>“Set Free” in BIO deletes the Ink from your iPad after you confirm. “Set All Inks Free” in Settings deletes every Ink, saved artwork and Canvas draft from your iPad and keeps your Artist Identity. Neither action has an undo, and neither sends the Ink anywhere.</p>
          <p>Deletion is permanent. Export anything you want to keep first.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="tokens">
          <span class="section-number">06</span><h2>Tokens and purchases</h2>
          <p>Digital Ink is free to download. Optional online features use tokens, which you can buy through Apple’s in-app purchase system. At the time of writing, an online image description costs 1 token and an AI memory reconstruction costs 10 tokens. Costs may change; the app shows the cost before you confirm.</p>
          <p>Tokens are units for using online services. They have no cash value, cannot be redeemed for money, and cannot be given or sold to other people. Tokens are not deducted unless you request an online operation. If an eligible operation fails after tokens were charged, the service attempts to return them automatically.</p>
          <p>Payments, refunds and purchase restoration are handled by Apple under its own terms. Your token balance is kept by Digital Ink’s online service against a pseudonymous service identifier. If that identifier is lost, or records are deleted at your request, a remaining balance may be impossible to verify or restore.</p>
          <p>For a problem with a purchase, email <a href="mailto:hello@q888.space">hello@q888.space</a> with your Apple transaction ID.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="online">
          <span class="section-number">07</span><h2>Online features and AI</h2>
          <p>Digital Ink works offline. Online Assist and AI Memory Reconstruction are optional, run through Digital Ink’s Cloudflare service and OpenAI, and ask for your permission before anything is sent. Buying tokens is not permission.</p>
          <p>Descriptions and generated images are produced automatically and can be wrong, incomplete or unexpected. A reconstruction is a new image inspired by what an Ink remembers; it is not a recovered photograph. Do not rely on them for anything important.</p>
          <p>Do not send material you have no right to share, or material that is unlawful. Online services depend on third parties, may be slow or unavailable, and may change or stop. Offline features keep working without them.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="verification">
          <span class="section-number">08</span><h2>Verification and provenance</h2>
          <p>Artwork verification and provenance records are made and checked locally on the device. They show what Digital Ink recorded; they do not prove facts that were never recorded. Heritage Inks, created before the current provenance system, keep their historical records as they are.</p>
          <p>Verification, certificates and exported files are not legal proof of authorship, ownership or value.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="use">
          <span class="section-number">09</span><h2>Acceptable use</h2>
          <p>Do not use Digital Ink to break the law, to infringe other people’s rights, or to harass others. Do not attempt to tamper with the app, bypass its limits or token system, duplicate Inks, forge provenance or signatures, or overload or attack the online services.</p>
          <p>Access to the online services may be limited or blocked if they are misused.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="liability">
          <span class="section-number">10</span><h2>Warranty and liability</h2>
          <p>Digital Ink is provided “as is”, as a personal art project, without promises that it will be error-free, always available or suitable for a particular purpose. Keep your own copies of work that matters to you.</p>
          <p>To the extent the law allows, the developer is not liable for indirect or consequential loss, or for loss of Inks, artworks or data caused by deletion, device loss or reset, a transfer you confirmed, or third-party services. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, or your statutory consumer rights.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="changes">
          <span class="section-number">11</span><h2>Changes and law</h2>
          <p>These terms may be updated when Digital Ink’s features or services change. The current version is published at q888.space/terms/ with a new effective date. If you keep using the app after a change, you accept the updated terms.</p>
          <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Scotland, without affecting any mandatory consumer rights you have where you live.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-contact">
          <span class="section-number">12</span><h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>For questions about these terms:</p>
          <address>Alexander Sestakovs<br />Email: <a href="mailto:hello@q888.space">hello@q888.space</a><br />Website: <a href="/dink/">q888.space/dink</a></address>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>

    <footer class="policy-footer">
      <div class="policy-shell"><p>Terms of use for Digital Ink. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a></p></div>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy-page{--ink:#181b20;--paper:#f0eee9;--blue:#2a68b4;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:system-ui,sans-serif}.policy-shell{width:min(1120px,calc(100% - 3rem));margin-inline:auto}.policy-hero{padding:clamp(9rem,15vw,13rem) 0 5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #cbc7bf;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#f3f1ec 60%,#dfe8f4)}.policy-kicker,.policy-toc>p{font-family:"Space Mono",monospace;color:var(--blue);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.18em}.policy-hero h1{font-family:"Space Grotesk",sans-serif;font-size:clamp(4.5rem,12vw,10rem);letter-spacing:-.075em;line-height:.74;margin:1.5rem 0 3rem}.policy-summary{max-width:800px;font-size:clamp(1.35rem,2.4vw,2rem);line-height:1.45;color:#444951}.policy-meta{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);margin:4rem 0 2rem;border-top:1px solid #b8b5af}.policy-meta div{padding:1rem 1rem 1rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #b8b5af}.policy-meta dt{font-family:"Space Mono";font-size:.65rem;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6f747b;margin-bottom:.6rem}.policy-meta dd{margin:0;font-weight:650}.policy-meta a,.policy-content a{color:var(--blue)}.policy-principles{display:flex;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.policy-principles span{border:1px solid #aeb5bd;border-radius:100px;padding:.55rem .8rem;font-size:.75rem}.policy-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:240px minmax(0,720px);gap:clamp(3rem,9vw,9rem);align-items:start;padding:6rem 0 8rem}.policy-toc{position:sticky;top:7rem}.policy-toc ol{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.5rem 0}.policy-toc li{border-top:1px solid #d2cfc8}.policy-toc a{display:block;padding:.62rem 0;color:#5f646c;text-decoration:none;font-size:.8rem}.policy-toc a:hover{color:var(--blue)}.policy-content section{scroll-margin-top:7rem;padding:0 0 4.5rem;margin:0 0 4.5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #c9c6bf}.policy-content .section-number{display:block;font-family:"Space Mono";font-size:.7rem;color:var(--blue);letter-spacing:.15em}.policy-content h2{font-family:"Space Grotesk",sans-serif;font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);letter-spacing:-.045em;line-height:1;margin:1rem 0 2rem}.policy-content h3{font-family:"Space Grotesk",sans-serif;font-size:1.3rem;margin:2rem 0 .6rem}.policy-content p,.policy-content li{font-size:1.03rem;line-height:1.75;color:#3f444b}.policy-content ul{padding-left:1.25rem}.policy-content li{padding:.2rem 0}.policy-emphasis{border-left:4px solid var(--blue);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;background:#e1e7ee;color:#17263a!important;font-weight:650}.policy-contact{border-bottom:0!important}.policy-contact address{font-style:normal;font-family:"Space Grotesk";font-size:1.4rem;line-height:1.7}.policy-footer{background:#161a20;color:#dbe0e7;padding:3rem 0}.policy-footer .policy-shell{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2rem}.policy-footer p{margin:0;color:#949ca8}.policy-footer a{color:#8ab8f0}
  @media(max-width:800px){.policy-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding-top:3rem}.policy-toc{position:static;border-bottom:1px solid #cbc7bf;padding-bottom:2rem}.policy-toc ol{columns:2}.policy-meta{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}
  @media(max-width:520px){.policy-shell{width:calc(100% - 2rem)}.policy-meta{grid-template-columns:1fr}.policy-toc ol{columns:1}.policy-footer .policy-shell{flex-direction:column}}
</style>
